  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## The Event
    
    The Rofundis∴rupt was the catastrophic fracture of the primary fire-core vein beneath ☽'scar Ramtatus~, a Nightshelf colony founded during the Great Thaw's expansion. The vein had supplied thermal energy to the colony's forges, warrens, and heating infrastructure for three generations, and its output underwrote the Nightshelf's fire-core exports under the Flipper Accord, the trade agreement binding the two penguin civilizations. The rupture occurred during the Faction Wars.
    
    The ice-memory at the relevant stratum records the event not as a detonation but as a cessation — the deep thermal hum that had vibrated through ☽'scar Ramtatus~ simply stopped. Miners located the breach at the colony's root: a fissure wide enough to lose a penguin in, venting heat into unmapped cavities below. Twelve miners were buried when the deepest section of the vein tore open, entombed under ice that geological surveys had classified as stone. They were found in charcoal wraps with fire-cores spilling from cracked containers around them.
    
    The fissure was sealed with bone-ash and prayer-silence. The heat did not return.
    
    ## Aftermath
    
    The collapse of the vein eliminated ☽'scar Ramtatus~'s primary thermal output. Fire-cores dimmed across the warren-levels. Forges went cold. Thermal vents that had kept the deepest caverns habitable ceased functioning. The Aurora Stack, the surface civilization dependent on fire-core imports, began hoarding remaining supply.
    
    Within the colony, the crisis followed a pattern I have seen repeated in ice-records from unrelated eras: rationing became theft, theft became violence, and families were forced to select which warren-members would be relocated to unheated cold-quarters so that warmth could be preserved for the young. The chronicles do not specify how many colonies failed to seal their own subsidiary fractures. The silence on this point is consistent across every source I have located.
    
    The Profun∴lapsum, a subsequent thermal rupture beneath Wane☽ Oncea — a separate Nightshelf mining site — compounded the losses. The Nightshelf's fire-core supply has never fully recovered.
    
    ## Commemoration
    
    The Rofundis∴rupt is preserved under Memoria∴moria, the Nightshelf memorial-law requiring disasters be carved into the colony's ice-walls, and observed during Ritus∴um, the commemorative gathering at which survivors display relics and speak the names of the dead.
    
    The tunnel-runner Kelm, who froze beside a sealed passage holding two fire-cores — one destined for the next mining shift, one for a child she had never met — survives in a Nightshelf counting rhyme. Fledglings tally fire-cores to zero and stamp their feet on *none*. The tunnel-mothers, when asked, refuse to say who Kelm was.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
