  annotation "note_1771595251837_1", anchor: "Twelve miners were buried", text: "Nightshelf deep-shifts at ☽'scar Ramtatus~ ran in crews of six. Twelve is two full rotations — plausible if both were below when the vein tore. But the Ritus∴um recitations I have cross-referenced name fourteen. The ice-memory at that stratum is too saturated with thermal shock to resolve individual presences. I let twelve stand because three sources converge on it. Fourteen may include two who died in the hours after.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771595251837_2", anchor: "The tunnel-mothers, when asked, refuse to say who Kelm was", text: "They know exactly who Kelm was. They will not say because saying would make the rhyme a history lesson, and history lessons can be revised. A counting game cannot. It simply is. The fledglings stamp their feet on *none* without knowing why, and that is precisely the mechanism by which the loss survives. The tunnel-mothers understood something about preservation that Memoria∴moria, for all its carved permanence, does not: the most durable archive is one that does not know it is an archive.", type: :commentary, display: :full
